 "summary": {
  "headline": "Diamond Power Q1 FY27 revenue rose 129% YoY to INR690 crore and PAT 191% to INR58.5 crore, with FY27 revenue guided at INR4,300-4,500 crore.",
  "overview": "Consolidated Q1 FY27 revenue was INR690 crore (up 129% YoY), EBITDA INR85 crore (up 172%, margin 12.3%, up about 200 bps) and PAT INR58.5 crore (up 191%, net margin 8.5%). Management attributed the quarter's weakness to early, heavy monsoon flooding in Gujarat, which it said cost an estimated INR70-80 crore of revenue. The QIP of INR1,614 crore closed in the quarter, moving net worth from negative INR922 crore to positive INR691 crore on a pro forma basis. Management reiterated FY27 revenue guidance of INR4,300-4,500 crore and FY28 of INR7,500 crore, with EBITDA margin guided at 11-13%.",
  "financial_highlights": [
   {
    "metric": "Consolidated revenue",
    "value": "INR690 crore (~$83 million)",
    "change": "+129% YoY"
   },
   {
    "metric": "EBITDA",
    "value": "INR85 crore; margin 12.3%",
    "change": "+172% YoY; margin up ~200 bps"
   },
   {
    "metric": "PAT",
    "value": "INR58.5 crore; net margin 8.5%",
    "change": "+191% YoY"
   },
   {
    "metric": "EPS",
    "value": "INR1.11 (face value INR1)",
    "change": ""
   },
   {
    "metric": "Order book (as on 11 Aug 2026)",
    "value": "INR3,688 crore (~$445 million), 12 product lines",
    "change": "~2x FY26 revenue; over INR1,000 crore fresh wins since April"
   },
   {
    "metric": "Net worth",
    "value": "Negative INR922 crore at 30 Jun 2026; positive INR691 crore pro forma post QIP",
    "change": ""
   },
   {
    "metric": "QIP proceeds",
    "value": "INR1,614-1,640 crore",
    "change": "Completed in Q1; full minimum public shareholding achieved"
   },
   {
    "metric": "Operating cost",
    "value": "6.5% of revenue",
    "change": "Down from 9% earlier; internal target 6%"
   }
  ],
  "segments": [
   {
    "name": "Medium voltage (11-66 kV) and EHV cables",
    "commentary": "Largest single block of order book; the INR435 crore data center order sits in this band. Management targets moving mix up the voltage curve; EBITDA guided at ~14-15% for 11 kV, ~16% for 33 kV and 18-22% for 66 kV and above."
   },
   {
    "name": "Low voltage cables",
    "commentary": "Q1 mix skewed to LV and conductor due to monsoon. New copper-focused LV plant (brownfield, from rod mill conversion) targets ~INR1,880 crore revenue potential at full utilization, commercial production FY27-28; EBITDA 8-9%."
   },
   {
    "name": "Conductors (incl. HTLS, AL-59)",
    "commentary": "Management stopped producing ACSR; AL-59 is ~70% of the market per management. Conductor EBITDA guided at 9-10%, with HTLS expected to run one or two notches above that."
   }
  ],
  "guidance_outlook": [
   "FY27 consolidated revenue guided at INR4,300-4,500 crore, implying ~INR1,200-1,250 crore per quarter over Q2-Q4 versus INR690 crore in Q1; management described the ramp as gradual, with Q4 the largest quarter.",
   "FY28 revenue target INR7,500 crore; management said FY29 INR14,000 crore is not a target and that INR14,000 crore is the peak potential of existing plus new capacity.",
   "EBITDA margin guidance 11-13% for FY27, dependent on metal prices and pass-through lags; management said FY28 margin would be maintained in this band with an aim to improve.",
   "Data center order target INR1,000 crore before 31 Mar 2027; data center sales of ~INR750 crore expected in FY27 and a target of ~INR1,500 crore in FY28 (~20% of revenue).",
   "Export order book target of at least INR500 crore by year end; export revenue currently 'very negligible', with US, Europe and Middle East certifications pending.",
   "Adani Group share of order book is 40%+; board mandate to reduce to ~20% by year end. Around 670 active customers and 200+ customers in the order book."
  ],
